# @clipy/transcribe

Converts speech from audio and video recordings into timestamped text segments using local speech recognition models or external transcription services.

## Requirements

- Node.js 20.19 or later
- pnpm
- FFmpeg installed and available on PATH

Check whether FFmpeg is installed:

```bash
ffmpeg -version
```

If FFmpeg is installed in a custom location, set the `CLIPY_FFMPEG` environment variable to its executable path.

Example for Windows:

```bat
set CLIPY_FFMPEG=C:\ffmpeg\bin\ffmpeg.exe
```

## Supported transcription providers

| Configuration kind | Provider |
|---|---|
| `none` | Transcription disabled |
| `local` | On-device transcription |
| `openai-compatible` | OpenAI-compatible API |
| `deepgram` | Deepgram |
| `assemblyai` | AssemblyAI |
| `elevenlabs` | ElevenLabs |
| `gemini` | Google Gemini |

## Usage

Import the public API:

```typescript
import {
  transcribe,
  downloadModel,
  modelStatus
} from "@clipy/transcribe";
```

### 1. Disable transcription

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "none"
});
```

This disables transcription and returns a gap covering the recording duration when available.

### 2. Local transcription

Local transcription runs a downloaded speech model on the user's machine.

```typescript
await downloadModel("english-fast");

const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "local",
  model: "english-fast"
});

console.log(result.segments);
```

### 3. OpenAI-compatible provider

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "openai-compatible",
  baseUrl: "https://api.openai.com/v1",
  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!,
  model: "whisper-1"
});
```

### 4. Deepgram

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "deepgram",
  apiKey: process.env.DEEPGRAM_API_KEY!
});
```

### 5. AssemblyAI

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "assemblyai",
  apiKey: process.env.ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY!
});
```

### 6. ElevenLabs

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "elevenlabs",
  apiKey: process.env.ELEVENLABS_API_KEY!
});
```

### 7. Google Gemini

```typescript
const result = await transcribe("recording.mp4", {
  kind: "gemini",
  apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY!
});
```

## Local models

The package supports two local transcription models:

| Model ID | Model | Download size |
|---|---|---|
| `english-fast` | NVIDIA Parakeet TDT-CTC 110M | Approximately 104 MB |
| `multilingual` | Whisper Base | Approximately 161 MB |

Local transcription uses `sherpa-onnx-node`, which must be provided by the host application.

### Download and check model status

```typescript
for (const model of ["english-fast", "multilingual"] as const) {
  const status = modelStatus(model);

  if (!status.installed) {
    await downloadModel(model);
  }

  console.log(modelStatus(model));
}
```

`modelStatus()` returns:

- `installed`: Whether the model is installed.
- `dir`: The model directory path.

`downloadModel()` downloads and verifies the model files using SHA-256 checksums. It returns the installed model directory.

## Transcription configuration

The `TranscriptionConfig` type supports:

- `none`: Disables transcription.
- `local`: Uses a downloaded local model.
- `openai-compatible`: Uses an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
- `deepgram`: Uses the Deepgram service.
- `assemblyai`: Uses AssemblyAI.
- `elevenlabs`: Uses ElevenLabs.
- `gemini`: Uses Google Gemini.

The hosted provider configurations require an API key. The OpenAI-compatible configuration requires a base URL, API key and model name.

## Transcription result

The `transcribe()` function returns a result containing:

- `segments`: Recognized text with start and end timestamps in milliseconds.
- `engine`: The transcription engine used.
- `language`: Language code when available.
- `gaps`: Intervals without transcript coverage.

Each transcript segment contains:

- `startMs`: Start time in milliseconds.
- `endMs`: End time in milliseconds.
- `text`: Recognized speech.

### Understanding gaps

A gap represents a portion of the recording that has no transcript.

Each gap contains:

- `startMs`: Gap start time.
- `endMs`: Gap end time.
- `reason`: Explanation for the missing transcript.

A gap does not necessarily mean silence.

For example:
- Transcription disabled can produce a gap covering the entire recording.
- A recording without an audio track can also produce a full-recording gap.
- Other gaps indicate portions without transcript coverage.

## FFmpeg requirement

FFmpeg is required to extract audio from video or audio files.

The package converts audio into a standard format:

- Sample rate: 16 kHz
- Channels: Mono
- Format: 16-bit PCM WAV

By default, FFmpeg must be available on PATH.

For a custom installation, configure `CLIPY_FFMPEG` with the full executable path.

## Privacy

The `none` and `local` configurations do not upload recording audio for transcription.

The following configurations send audio to their configured external services:

- OpenAI-compatible
- Deepgram
- AssemblyAI
- ElevenLabs
- Gemini

Local model downloads require an internet connection, but the recording audio is processed on the local machine.

Keep API keys secure. Use environment variables and never commit secret keys to the repository.

## Additional options

The `transcribe()` function accepts optional settings:

- `signal`: Allows cancellation using an AbortSignal.
- `modelDir`: Specifies a custom local model directory.
- `onProgress`: Receives extraction, download and transcription progress.
- `speechEngine`: Specifies the sherpa-onnx-node entry file for local transcription.

